   7:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  *
   8:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  * This file contains simple error-reporting and trace-message routines.
   9:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  * These are suitable for Unix-like systems and others where writing to
  10:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  * stderr is the right thing to do.  Many applications will want to replace
  11:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  * some or all of these routines.
  12:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  *
  13:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  * If you define USE_WINDOWS_MESSAGEBOX in jconfig.h or in the makefile,
  14:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  * you get a Windows-specific hack to display error messages in a dialog box.
  15:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  * It ain't much, but it beats dropping error messages into the bit bucket,
  16:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  * which is what happens to output to stderr under most Windows C compilers.
  17:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  *
  18:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  * These routines are used by both the compression and decompression code.
  19:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c ****  */
  20:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jerror.c **** 
